{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Abraham said to Sarah his wife, She is my sister.</b> This was not like what happened in Egypt, for there, when they came to Egypt, the Egyptians saw the woman, that she was beautiful, and they praised her to the officials and to the king, for they are men of licentiousness. But this king was blameless and upright, and his men too were good; only Abraham suspected them, and he would say to everyone, She is my sister." "<b>And Abimelech sent and took, etc.</b> Now this is a wonder, that Sarah after having grown old was beautiful exceedingly, so that kings would take her. For when she was taken to Pharaoh, if she was sixty-five years old, it is possible that her appearance was still upon her. But after she had grown old and the way of women had ceased from her — this is a wonder. Perhaps she returned to her youth, as the angel announced to her, according to the words of our Sages (Bava Metzi'a 87a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:36.159803536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}